.\" Title: vrw-stop
.\" Author: vrw contributors
.\" Manual section: 1
.\" Process this file with
.\"   groff -man -Tascii vrw-stop.1

.TH VRW\-STOP 1 "2025" "vrw" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
vrw\-stop \- gracefully shut down a running vrw instance

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrw
\fBstop\fR [\fIPID\fR] [\fB\-\-interactive\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Gracefully shut down a running vrw instance by sending an HTTP \fBPOST /api/shutdown\fR request to its API. This allows the instance to clean up resources, kill all managed commands (using the configured exit timeout), flush logs, and exit cleanly. If no PID is given and exactly one instance is running, that instance is stopped automatically.

The shutdown process kills all running commands with SIGINT (followed by SIGKILL after the configured \fB\-\-exit\-timeout\fR), removes the instance from the registry, and terminates the HTTP server. This is the recommended way to stop vrw instances, as it ensures proper cleanup of pseudo-terminals and temporary files.

If the instance is unresponsive (e.g., frozen process, network issue, or stale registry entry), the command may time out. In that case, use \fBkill(1)\fR or \fBkill \-9\fR as a fallback to force-terminate the process.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR \-\-interactive
Present a numbered list of running instances and let the user select
which ones to stop by typing space-separated numbers (e.g. "1 3 5").
Requires a terminal (stdin must be a TTY).

.SH ARGUMENTS

.TP
.B PID
Process ID of the vrw instance to stop. If omitted and exactly one instance is registered, it is stopped automatically. If omitted and multiple instances are running, an error is displayed listing the available instances.

.SH EXAMPLES

.PP
Stop a specific instance:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrw list\fR
INSTANCE  PID: 12345  PORT: 9090  BIND: 127.0.0.1  DAEMON: no  DISPLAY: yes
INSTANCE  PID: 12346  PORT: 8080  BIND: 127.0.0.1  DAEMON: yes  DISPLAY: no

\fB$ vrw stop 12346\fR
Sent shutdown request to PID 12346 (port 8080)
.fi
.RE

.PP
Stop the only running instance (PID omitted):
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrw stop\fR
Sent shutdown request to PID 12345 (port 9090)
.fi
.RE

.PP
Equivalent curl:
.RS
.PP
.nf
curl -s -X POST http://localhost:9090/api/shutdown
.fi
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
Shutdown request sent successfully.

.TP
.B 1
Error (instance not found, connection refused, multiple instances without PID, etc.).

.SH SEE ALSO

.BR vrw (1),
.BR vrw\-list (1),
.BR vrw\-stop\-command (1),
.BR kill (1)
